# Golden bytes: login handshake packet body, protocol 775, address "localhost",
# port 25565, intent 2 (login). Hand-assembled from the wire spec; the test
# decodes it and compares re-encoded output byte-for-byte.
#
# **Hand-assembled, but checked against a real client.** These are the only golden bytes in the tree written
# from a reading of the spec rather than captured, which is the shape every confirmed failure of the P00-P09
# review round has had: an expectation written from the same understanding as the code it checks, so the two
# agree whether or not either is right. A real 26.1.2 handshake, captured through the rig, is
#
#   00 87 06 09 31 32 37 2e 30 2e 30 2e 31 63 eb 02
#
# -- the same encoding with "127.0.0.1" and port 25579: identical in every field the test exercises, differing
# only in the two values that must differ. So this fixture agrees with the wire and not merely with our reader
# of it. See docs/vanilla-parity/PARITY-MATRIX.md.
87 06
09 6C 6F 63 61 6C 68 6F 73 74
63 DD
02
